***REMOVED*** Example environment configuration for structural-isomorphism.
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED*** Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored
***REMOVED*** (see .gitignore) — never commit your real keys.
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED*** Usage:
***REMOVED***     cp .env.example .env
***REMOVED***     ***REMOVED*** edit .env, fill in real keys
***REMOVED***     set -a; source .env; set +a
***REMOVED***     python v4/scripts/b3_ensemble.py ...
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED*** Or use a process manager like `direnv` / `dotenv-cli` to auto-load.

***REMOVED*** ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
***REMOVED*** LLM provider keys
***REMOVED*** ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

***REMOVED*** DeepSeek direct API (used by v4/scripts/b3_ensemble.py and
***REMOVED*** v4/product/d1_phase_detector/extract_structtuple.py).
***REMOVED*** Get a key at https://platform.deepseek.com.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

***REMOVED*** OpenRouter (optional fallback router for cross-vendor ensemble; CN region
***REMOVED*** may be blocked — see paper appendix).
***REMOVED*** OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your-key-here

***REMOVED*** ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
***REMOVED*** Optional configuration
***REMOVED*** ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

***REMOVED*** Override DeepSeek default model (v4/scripts/b3_ensemble.py respects this).
***REMOVED*** DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro

***REMOVED*** Override DeepSeek base URL (for self-hosted proxies / region failover).
***REMOVED*** DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions

***REMOVED*** ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
***REMOVED*** Web backend (web/backend) — launch hardening knobs
***REMOVED*** ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

***REMOVED*** Deployment environment. "prod" disables /docs /redoc /openapi.json and
***REMOVED*** requires STRUCTURAL_SHARE_TOKEN_SECRET to be set. Default: dev.
***REMOVED*** STRUCTURAL_ENV=prod

***REMOVED*** Daily LLM-call circuit breaker (launch P0-2). Total LLM-backed requests
***REMOVED*** (/api/ask + /api/analyze) allowed per UTC day before the service returns
***REMOVED*** a friendly 429. <= 0 disables the cap (NOT recommended in prod).
***REMOVED*** Default: 500.
***REMOVED*** STRUCTURAL_LLM_DAILY_CALL_CAP=500

***REMOVED*** /api/analyze out-of-scope similarity floor (launch P1-3). A query-mode
***REMOVED*** analyze request whose query-vs-KB cosine is below this is declined
***REMOVED*** instead of generating a report. Default: 0.30 (deliberately lax — the
***REMOVED*** deterministic trivial/chit-chat detector is the primary gate).
***REMOVED*** ANALYZE_SCOPE_MIN_SIMILARITY=0.30
